|desc=If the character is struck by a potentially lethal blow, he makes a [[reflex]] [[saving throw]] ([[difficulty class|DC]] = damage dealt). If successful, he takes only half damage from the blow.
|use=automatic, but limited to one use per [[day]]. [[Flat-foot]]ed characters cannot make a ''defensive roll''.
|icon=ife_dodgeroll.gif
|bonus1=rogue
|class1=shadowdancer
}}__NOTOC__

==Notes==

*This feat is only available to a rogue as a bonus feat, not as a [[general feat]]. Shadowdancers receive it automatically at level 5.
* A "potentially lethal blow" refers to a standard attack with a [[weapon]] that would&ndash;if not for this feat&ndash;reduce the target below one [[hit point]] with just its [[physical damage]].
* Nonphysical damage is ignored by this feat. Nonphysical damage is not included when determining if a blow is lethal, when calculating the DC, nor when damage is halved.

===Previous versions===

*Prior to version 1.69, there was no limit to how many times per day this feat would be used, despite the in-game description saying it could only be used once per day.

